    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Callīpĭdes</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Callipp-</span></b> ), ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλλιππιδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Grecian runner who
				made no progress</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quem cursitare ac ne cubiti quidem mensuram
					progredi proverbio Graeco notatum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 38</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 13, 12, 3</span></i>.</div>
